# Box-wide tool credentials, sourced by every shell (~/.bashrc.d/devbox.sh).
# Bootstrap installs this template as ~/.config/devbox/secrets.env at mode 600
# and never fills it; it lives on the bind mount, so it survives every rebuild.
#
# Plain KEY=value pairs only - no `export`, no `op://` references. The container
# holds no 1Password account by design (docs/secrets.md): render values on the
# laptop, where approving access is yours to do, and copy them in.
#
# What belongs here: credentials every project shares, i.e. the tools' own.
# What does not: anything a single project needs. Project secrets go in that
# project's .env so a leak stays scoped to one project - GCP included, since
# each project has its own GCP project and therefore its own ADC key path.

# GitHub CLI. Fine-grained, expiring, and read-mostly: contents/actions/checks
# read for dashboards and pipelines, issues or pull-requests write only if
# agents should post. `git push` never needs it - that goes over SSH.
# GH_TOKEN=github_pat_...

# Models used by OMP itself, as opposed to a project's own LLM calls.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
